## Provider Configuration

### OpenAI

| Variable | Description | Required? |
| :--- |:---| :--- |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | Your secret OpenAI API key. Alternative: use `/auth login openai-codex` for OAuth. | **Yes*** |
| `OPENAI_MODEL` | The model to use. E.g.: `gpt-5.6-sol`, `gpt-5.6-luna`, `gpt-5.4`, `gpt-4o`. | No |
| `OPENAI_ASSISTANT_MODEL` | The model to use specifically for the Assistants API. | No |
| `OPENAI_USE_RESPONSES` | Set to `true` to force the `v1/responses` API for every model. Setting `false` does not force `v1/chat/completions`: OAuth sessions and models whose catalog entry prefers the Responses API (e.g. `gpt-5.4`) still use it. | No |
| `OPENAI_API_URL` | Custom Chat Completions endpoint. Must be the full URL ending in `/chat/completions`; the `/models` listing URL is derived from it. With a custom host the model listing is not filtered by family, and `OPENAI_API_KEY` is still sent as the Bearer token (set it to the gateway's key). | No |
| `OPENAI_RESPONSES_API_URL` | Custom Responses API endpoint. Set both URLs when redirecting the provider to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint. | No |
| `OPENAI_MAX_TOKENS` | Sets the maximum tokens to use in the session (depends on model) | No

