| `CHATCLI_MEMORY_FALLBACK_PROVIDERS` | Fallback provider chain for **memory extraction** (e.g. `OPENAI,GOOGLEAI`). Empty → falls back to `CHATCLI_FALLBACK_PROVIDERS`. Segments that fail every provider are queued on disk and retried. | — |
| `CHATCLI_SELFEVOLVE_MODE` | Self-evolution of skills, riding the same memory-extraction pass. `auto` authors/evolves skills on its own (edit-safe, reversible via `@skill restore`); `suggest` only suggests; `off` disables. See `/config selfevolve`. | `auto` |
| `CHATCLI_GRAPH_INDEX` | Injects the knowledge-graph index card (map-of-content) into the prompt each turn — chat, agent and coder. Served from the persisted graph cache (see `CHATCLI_MEMORY_GRAPH`), deterministic / cache-friendly. The pull path via `@memory neighbors`/`map` stays available regardless of this flag. | `on` |

